r=a.add('workbook',12,'Standalone activity materials: catalogue B version 1 is B1 Bookmark drawing (10 min, quiet Yes), B2 Story circle (8 min, quiet No), B3 Pattern puzzle (12 min, quiet Yes), B4 Tower challenge (15 min, quiet No), in that order. Valid whole minutes are 0–30 and Quiet required is Yes/No. A fit requires time≤available minutes AND (quiet not required OR activity quiet). P1 version 1: Card 1 validates both fields, clarifies invalid input and stops, otherwise starts marker at B1 with cleared output. Card 2 checks both conditions, records them and stops with the first fitting row and reason. Card 3 advances one row after failure and returns to Card 2, or stops with no match after the last row fails. Start every new request at Card 1. Save request, catalogue/instruction versions, expected result and actual trace separately.')
a.common('Build a new route through a small catalogue','Build runnable instruction cards, predict from the contract and preserve actual state, outputs and stopping reasons.',[(12,'W1 · Make complete prototype materials','Use the supplied standalone catalogue and instruction-card reference.'),(13,'W2 · Predict, hand over and record the run','Keep the expected result separate from actual operator steps.'),(14,'W3 · Diagnose and version an instruction defect','Preserve the original failure and label the changed instructions.'),(16,'W5 · Save enough evidence to inspect the result','Retain requests, versions, expected outputs and actual traces.')], 'For the partner-as-computer activity run, required expectations are B2 for (9,No), B1 for (11,No), no match for (7,No), and clarification for (blank,Yes). Actual observations must be collected from the operator, not copied from these expected answers. P1 explicitly resets each request at B1 with cleared output; skipping that step is an execution mistake. A saved instruction version that omits a needed rule has an instruction defect. Keep original traces, label reruns and version edits. These paper rules do not constitute a trained model or establish software reliability. Reserve Build a new route through a small catalogue for an individual first attempt.',{12:[r]})
